#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128880 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c28b8ae-71ef-5d26-895a-5d949fc5b164" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "6bba4758-678a-5bf6-b9df-cdc2662ab306" :question/math-academy-id "e-5525" :question/problem "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/3e677aa7f2db1cc637e0566a60813ebae1e2bccf80325106317c1d2b7717c2a5.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/67a421166c674275ae14da43962c8e5c8ea37b6a9c8a0548d5b09428b703d831.png) are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/fde83769f627e95f5dfe3285bf275ebfe1678710a36c264b6662248063470bb0.png) then what is the value of $ad+eh?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & -5-7\\text{i} \\\\ 1-6\\text{i} & 5-9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -7 \\\\ -6 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $a=2,d=5,e=-3$ and $h=-9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nad+eh=2 \\cdot 5 + (-3) \\cdot (-9) = 37.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128881 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations to a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "0f32e78f-a13d-5e81-ba64-bff28a61aacf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5526" :question/problem "Given the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/766ddf98a05c69ef0791858a7f32457425cf1a9650d2205227ffc7d9d173d2e7.png) find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{\\textrm{i}}R_1, \\qquad R_2 := R_2 - 2\\textrm{i}R_1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the row operations to $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} & -\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\, &  & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\, &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2\\text{i}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/9fef320d53c15c2820719bb1d0dfabb00afa6200b43279e3137fbb25c4e67e2d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128909 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Complex Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "27f2c303-b9a9-5337-bcea-865a9273b35b" :question/math-academy-id "e-5902" :question/problem "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/b696bb055794a4ff94c86abc39ef3929113f82683b548a933fc1103245eff3fc.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/e6a5f5644ae4bcdfca4ca26bb258f33378381737ee036142c1e1c24f568ad2ed.png), then what is $AB?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} & \\text{i} \\\\ 1 & 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-\\text{i})\\cdot (1+2\\text{i})+\\text{i}\\cdot \\text{i} & (-\\text{i})\\cdot (1-\\text{i})+\\text{i}\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1\\cdot (1+2\\text{i})+2\\text{i}\\cdot \\text{i} & 1\\cdot (1-\\text{i})+2\\text{i}\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2-\\text{i})+(-1) & (-1-\\text{i})+2\\text{i} \\\\ (1+2\\text{i})+(-2) & (1-\\text{i})+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -1+\\text{i} \\\\ -1+2\\text{i} & 1+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128910 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7c1b7ad-e4bf-55b2-8665-2cf35e402946" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "e8bc731b-bb0b-5a07-89d9-6acc9beebc82" :question/math-academy-id "e-5903" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overline{A},$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/25ce0cd375da320d1615cf49f659ec33e4646cf6bc66455198bec5fd591b3dd3.png) What is the value of $b_{11} + b_{23}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i} & 3-\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2-2\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & 3\\text{i} & 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{2-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1+2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4\\text{i} & 3+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} & 1-2\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} & -3\\text{i} & -2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b_{11} + b_{23} = (-4\\textrm{i}) + (1-2\\textrm{i}) = 1-6\\textrm{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129647 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations to a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "937e7ecb-5d77-505e-a76c-46c702d21a7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127677} {:answer/id #uuid "93edd233-da7b-598a-94e0-4bdecd43e6e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\textrm{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127678} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2c84f0-ea43-59b5-9f39-f9b287c237b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127679} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc717fd-8668-5fac-880a-295a4ac24690" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ 2\\textrm{i} & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127680} {:answer/id #uuid "2e725b4a-9a4d-5c6d-af11-5472379222ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad2c84f0-ea43-59b5-9f39-f9b287c237b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127679} :answer-field/id #uuid "04cbad56-afe9-56dd-b327-d0b3664c9323" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82b32e6d-28e5-58d1-919e-cc85298dd3c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-39014" :question/problem "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}]$, find the result of applying to $A$ the following  elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}-1}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}={R}_{2}-2\\text{i}{R}_{1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}-1}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2\\text{i}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324398 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7c1b7ad-e4bf-55b2-8665-2cf35e402946" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5ab1397-1508-5917-9175-f478087ddc1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324400} {:answer/id #uuid "f5633dd5-5eea-5a0a-8958-75fb99f9eb48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324401} {:answer/id #uuid "bd7bca6c-6e01-53eb-a364-0768e0c88416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11+5\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324402} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d9cf17-ec23-509d-afbd-61bc434e69e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14-58\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324403} {:answer/id #uuid "00176072-22c6-5d0a-becf-fa4e144a9abd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00176072-22c6-5d0a-becf-fa4e144a9abd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324404} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2019caf-3516-5dff-8648-f73726520627" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d5d20da-974d-5024-90da-ba1db4147536" :question/math-academy-id "q-76059" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where $A=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\text{i} & 6+4\\text{i} \\\\ 7-4\\text{i} & 4+9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$ What is the value of ${b}_{12}-{b}_{21}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}7-\\text{i} & 6+4\\text{i} \\\\ 7-4\\text{i} & 4+9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{7-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{6+4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{7-4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{4+9\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7+\\text{i} & 6-4\\text{i} \\\\ 7+4\\text{i} & 4-9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{12}-{b}_{21}=(6-4\\text{i})-(7+4\\text{i})=-1-8\\text{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324412 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c28b8ae-71ef-5d26-895a-5d949fc5b164" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f9c59ca-2a18-5b16-96e9-8efec5745ba1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324414} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb196bb-7dc6-554e-9e65-cc90a276eab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324415} {:answer/id #uuid "4c291387-b63d-50cd-b8eb-edc5fa774e84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324416} {:answer/id #uuid "b7635561-dac0-5029-a31d-38a4af5a0e6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324417} {:answer/id #uuid "a09c222d-a05d-5683-b929-deea4abf6c53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c291387-b63d-50cd-b8eb-edc5fa774e84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324416} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cfc46d9-0938-5c5f-b702-2595aa055b0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "58793c96-ddf8-519d-986f-39d6955284e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-76204" :question/problem "Find the real part of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 7-6\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} & 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 7-6\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 7-6\\text{i} \\\\ 0-\\text{i} & 4+0\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Re}(A)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Complex Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5445583-7cae-5d34-a67f-70614754b2b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4+6\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} \\\\ 8+6\\text{i} & -1-13\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324442} {:answer/id #uuid "29cb5c79-d63b-59bb-b68b-45ad61d4c9e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1+13\\text{i} & 7+5\\text{i} \\\\ 8+6\\text{i} & 4+6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324443} {:answer/id #uuid "b5d2e190-17b2-51b3-8319-9ba4fed94cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4+6\\text{i} & 8+6\\text{i} \\\\ 7-5\\text{i} & -1-13\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324444} {:answer/id #uuid "9ccc9e15-75bb-5c9c-bd71-373a223c949f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1-13\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} \\\\ 8+6\\text{i} & 4+6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324445} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf260e0-032f-5d9c-9b90-01c4a971c948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1-13\\text{i} & 8+6\\text{i} \\\\ 7-5\\text{i} & 4+6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ccc9e15-75bb-5c9c-bd71-373a223c949f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1-13\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} \\\\ 8+6\\text{i} & 4+6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324445} :answer-field/id #uuid "08dc7d36-4aab-51b3-b8c0-45d260b89c34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e93d1f28-d0c0-5126-b248-ca6895657c64" :question/math-academy-id "q-76223" :question/problem "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} & -1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\text{i} & 3+\\text{i} \\\\ -1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $AB=$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} & -1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3-\\text{i} & 3+\\text{i} \\\\ -1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(1-3\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})+(-1+2\\text{i})(-1+\\text{i}) & (1-3\\text{i})(3+\\text{i})+(-1+2\\text{i})(1-\\text{i}) \\\\ (2+2\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})+(1-\\text{i})(-1+\\text{i}) & (2+2\\text{i})(3+\\text{i})+(1-\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10\\text{i}+(-1-3\\text{i}) & (6-8\\text{i})+(1+3\\text{i}) \\\\ (8+4\\text{i})+2\\text{i} & (4+8\\text{i})+(-2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1-13\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} \\\\ 8+6\\text{i} & 4+6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations to a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88467948-7c2f-5183-a55b-6a11764ec90c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324449} {:answer/id #uuid "3221ed64-5409-52bc-9591-d74209d70c98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324450} {:answer/id #uuid "c931d64d-6af8-544b-8df9-3b976ea8c2ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324451} {:answer/id #uuid "70ac948a-9451-501c-af4c-8e9122449559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324452} {:answer/id #uuid "a007df91-53d7-5825-be0f-7622672a4954" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3221ed64-5409-52bc-9591-d74209d70c98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324450} :answer-field/id #uuid "77ab877a-ecbd-5dc3-82